  "starter": "-- Write your SQL query below\n\n",
  "statementHtml": "\n<p>Table: <code>Logs</code></p>\n<div class=\"statement-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Column Name</th><th>Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>log_id</td><td>int</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>log_id is the column of unique values for this table.<br/>Each row of this table contains the ID in a log Table.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Write a solution to find the start and end number of continuous ranges in the table <code>Logs</code>.</p>\n<p>Return the result table ordered by <code>start_id</code>.</p>\n<p>The result format is in the following example.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<p>Input: <br/>Logs table:</p><div class=\"statement-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>log_id</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Output:</p><div class=\"statement-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>start_id</th><th>end_id</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Explanation: <br/>The result table should contain all ranges in table Logs.<br/>From 1 to 3 is contained in the table.<br/>From 4 to 6 is missing in the table<br/>From 7 to 8 is contained in the table.<br/>Number 9 is missing from the table.<br/>Number 10 is contained in the table.</p>\n",
